e":"2016-02-09T10:16:59-08:00","id":826914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826040-heretical-coils-of-the-ordo?p=826905#post826905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Twilight Judge can go &quot;yo, Heretical Coil #1298564 is totally cool for peeps to study&quot;, and everyone else has to abide by that decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. They have to abide about as much as when a Prince declares an edict or an Elder forbids something. The Twilight Judge declaring Ziva as a really awesome Mystery would be found dead rather quickly by &quot;unknown forces&quot;. Bonus points if he's found Diablerized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:07:27-08:00","id":826982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826040-heretical-coils-of-the-ordo?p=826914#post826914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. They have to abide about as much as when a Prince declares an edict or an Elder forbids something. The Twilight Judge declaring Ziva as a really awesome Mystery would be found dead rather quickly by &quot;unknown forces&quot;. Bonus points if he's found Diablerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing so loses your killers dots in Status (Ordo Dracul). <i>Your decisions are sacrosanct</i>. <i>That is what the merit does</i>.<br /> <br /> Taking that merit signals to the other players that the rest of the Ordo trusts you enough to defer to your judgement.<br /> <br /> Now, a wide-spanning &quot;alright, Ziva is Okey-Dokey&quot; will probably result in a couple other Twilight Judges deciding that you're wrong, but saying that &quot;my friend here is worthy to learn the Mystery of the Wyrm&quot;? Less likely to be kiboshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:29:07-08:00","id":826997,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, if other Sanctified find out that one of their own has dedicated himself to the heresies of the Dracula Cult, that would probably be grounds for the Judge's Sanctified pal to lose some covenant status, at the very least. As far as I understand it, most of the Sanctified hold their beliefs to be incompatible with the teachings of the Ordo Dracul. Even setting theological debates aside, the political fallout would be pretty significant, as the local Bishop would likely have trouble trusting the loyalty of one of the clergy who took a member of a rival covenant as a mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T22:05:05-08:00","id":829580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826040-heretical-coils-of-the-ordo?p=826997#post826997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if other Sanctified find out that one of their own has dedicated himself to the heresies of the Dracula Cult, that would probably be grounds for the Judge's Sanctified pal to lose some covenant status, at the very least. As far as I understand it, most of the Sanctified hold their beliefs to be incompatible with the teachings of the Ordo Dracul. Even setting theological debates aside, the political fallout would be pretty significant, as the local Bishop would likely have trouble trusting the loyalty of one of the clergy who took a member of a rival covenant as a mentor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, considering that the Sanctified would <i>already</i> be performing a Miracle that puts them on the Sanctified &quot;BURN THE HERETIC SATANIST&quot; list? (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Pledge To The Worthless One</a>).<br /> <br /> That's kinda the <i>point</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:46:59-08:00","id":834969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/826040-heretical-coils-of-the-ordo?p=826151#post826151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a Coil that capitalized on worsening the Banes of <i>other</i> vampires? Probably that wouldn't be nearly hardline enough to worry most Ordo, but I could see a philosophical or political argument to get it declared Heresy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Deucalion do.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wqw3fchpaffj3dw/Deucalion.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s my take on them in the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}